    "legend": "A 3-year-old girl presented with cutaneous mastocytosis, absolute lymphopenia, elevated serum tryptase (60&nbsp;&micro;g/L), and <em>KIT</em> p.D816V mutation in peripheral blood using a high sensitivity PCR assay. Bone marrow biopsy showed a normocellular marrow with rare multifocal mast cell aggregates and increased interstitial mast cells, occupying 10% of cellular marrow, best demonstrated by immunohistochemical staining for KIT (CD117), CD25 (shown here), and tryptase.",
