    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "Gastrointestinal systemic mastocytosis",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "A 5-year-old girl presented with diarrhoea and abdominal pain necessitating repeat visits to the emergency room. Immunohistochemical staining for tryptase in a colon biopsy is dim to negative. Not shown: CD25 also marked the mast cell infiltrate; a bone marrow examination found rare spindle-shaped mast cells on aspirate smear, but the bone marrow biopsy lacked any significant mast cell aggregates, with only rare normal round mast cells, suggesting occult bone marrow involvement by systemic mastocytosis.",
